t(46, 2445, """My Muslim brother: do not treat the conduct of the Prophet ﷺ superficially! This saying, firmly established in its chain and agreed upon as authentic, going back to Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, is not merely a depiction of the greatness of the Prophet's ﷺ character and his overlooking every small thing, and all of that is true, but there is another dimension""")

t(47, 60, """.. there is the mind of the Prophet ﷺ and his great pure soul. 10 years is a very long period in which hundreds of daily events occur between the Prophet and his servant, not a short period! That 10 years pass and the Prophet ﷺ never said a single word of annoyance to his servant is a great and clear moral aspect, but there is another great dimension besides morals, which is not the axis of this post.

A great mind and a pure soul like this express a matter which, if a man adorned himself with it in every time and place, he would be of great standing among people, even if his enemies accused him of what is not in him, he would not care!

This noble Prophetic conduct of mind and soul addresses these "men" in every age and says to them:

🔴 Where are those who stand inside kitchens telling their wives: put salt on this, and cut the onion this way?!
🔴 Where are those who dislike the food served to them and constantly comment on the salt and other than salt?!
🔴 Where are those who stop at every small thing and do not pass over it, and classify it as among the greatest of major sins?!
🔴 Where are those who push themselves every day into women's issues and chores in the houses?!
🔴 Where are those who busy themselves with trivialities and superficialities and chase them around the clock?!
🔴 Where are those who get angry like children at everything that happens around them?!
🔴 Where are those who stop at "the slightest thing" in everything and seek pretexts, wasting the life, time and effort of the people around them?!
🔴 Where are those who wake up in the morning having decided to harm others in every possible way, and this is their chief occupation in life and the message they carry, instead of having a real godly message?!

And more than all this .. daily behavioral disasters that men and women are more obliged to watch for in themselves, for our Prophet ﷺ is a model not only for men but for men and women. This very brief presentation in explaining the noble Prophetic conduct with the Messenger's servant Anas ibn Malik is a presentation by which dozens of daily behavioral disasters in the lives of men and women can be measured .. Our Prophet is our model not only in words, O nation of words, except those on whom Allah the Exalted has mercy! Enough of the words in which we have become the masters of the world!""")

h(47, 1700, """This is the master of men, so let men learn. Anas said: "I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never once said to me 'Uff', nor said of anything I did: Why did you do it? nor of anything I left: Why did you leave it?" """)

