t(50, 1000, """Why do we fast on the Day of Arafah? Fasting is among the best of deeds, one of the best deeds, and it is a means of nearness to Allah the Exalted.
From Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: "I never saw the Messenger of Allah fasting in the ten." And it is a hadith with no defect in its chain.

As for the ten of Dhu al-Hijjah, they are great days among the days of Allah the Exalted, our Great Lord, and his ﷺ saying is established in its chain: "There are no days in which righteous deeds are dearer to Allah than these days," and fasting is one of the greatest righteous deeds. So know, may Allah preserve you, that the Ummah does not fast as a Sunnah from the Prophet ﷺ, for he never fasted on any of the days of the ten in his life; rather it is because his ﷺ saying is established with a sound chain, as in al-Bukhari: "There are no days in which righteous deeds are dearer to Allah than these days." That is because [the hadith of his ﷺ fasting on the Day of Arafah] in Muslim is a hadith with a weak chain; al-Bukhari, may Allah have mercy on him, found its chain defective and rejected it in its chain, and a number of hadith scholars also rejected it, so it is not established from the Prophet ﷺ.""")

